  "problem": "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{4+1}}{4+1}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{5}}{5}-\\frac{{1}^{5}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
